{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344168-help-me-stat-mela-the-elemental-dragon-of-air","id":1344168,"title":"Help me stat Mela the Elemental Dragon of Air","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-28T04:53:10-07:00","id":1344168,"title":"Help me stat Mela the Elemental Dragon of Air","content":"Fimbulwinter grips the land, and Ragnarok has begun; it seems the Second Age is ending, the Realm has (apparently) been destroyed, and Mela (apparently) now attempts to choke the entire world in ice... for somewhat unclear reasons. (Possibly Hesiesh is dead. And/or Pasiap. One PC thinks Pasiap has killed Mela and replaced her and is trying to destroy the world because he's angry humans keep pooping on his head. The other PCs are unconvinced. Possibly this is all Raksha lies or something.)<br /> <br /> So my PCs have travelled from their homeland north of Iscomay all the way to the Haslanti city of Crystal (via wooden-wyld-whale-tentacled-ship), where they're just in the process of hiring an airship. Next session (assuming they don't get into some random trouble or something) they'll be leaving Crystal to fly across the Wasting Tundra, and then to the Elemental Pole of Air to Mela's floating ice palace beyond the edge of the world.<br /> <br /> Then they will attempt to talk Mela down/rescue Mela from her evil brother/punch her in the face.<br /> <br /> And if they try and punch Mela, or just social-fu her, she'll need stats.<br /> <br /> <br /> My thought is to start with Fakharu (an Essence 6 Dragon), but with these changes:<br /> All water-aspected effects become air-aspected. For instance, River-Drinking Renewal becomes Storm-Inhaling Renewal, consuming gale-force winds, downpours, and/or heavy fog instead of water; Drowning-in-Coils Constriction asphyxiates by pulling air out of the target\u2019s lungs; and Flowing Body Dispersal turns the dragon\u2019s body gaseous. Seven Venoms Exhalation could breathe lightning instead.<br /> I can also give her the charms of the Storm Serpent: Fulminating Blast, Thunderous Rebuke, Evaporating Defence (which is actually really good), and Live Wire.<br /> <br /> Also, of course I can just increase her dice pools, soak, etc. I think maybe Essence 9 would be suitable for one of the five Elemental Dragons?<br /> <br /> But the numbers are easy, the hard thing is the charms. Maybe I should give her an excellency-like charm, like Octavian and Ahlat have. And should she have charms for, say, social influence, or just giant dice pools? Maybe charms to defend her main intimacies, so it's difficult to make her betray Gaia or stop all winds from moving or something fundamentally opposed to being the Elemental Dragon of Air.<br /> <br /> Any ideas?<br /> <br /> (A small note; my aim is to make her really powerful. It's not specifically for her to be able to wipe the floor with PCs. I mean, obviously the first might lead to the second, but I don't think she needs, say, an Overwhelming Negator, which a lack of is a big defence hole against a pack of Exalts. But that's fine, obviously groups of Exalts defeated Third-Circle Devas all over the place in the Divine Revolution. If they fight her, I want them to go &quot;oh shit, she's really powerful&quot; but she doesn't need to be amazing at exploiting the combat system itself, if you see what I mean. She's an Air Dragon, not an Invincible Sword Princess.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T05:48:43-07:00","id":1344171,"title":"","content":"I see two significant advantages for her from this set-up.<br /> <br /> #1 She can fly and can thus disengage pretty effortlessly from attackers who can't meet her in the air and makes it easier for her to focus on a single target such as for example, an airship forcing some of the PCs to go on the defensive if they don't want to risk crashing and burning.<br /> #2 If she's initiating Fimbulwinter she\u2019ll probably be a significant cold based environmental hazard coupled with serious visibility penalties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T06:02:02-07:00","id":1344173,"title":"","content":"I wonder if there wouldn\u2019t be some merit in looki BG at Air Dragon Style for some inspiration, as it\u2019s theoretically based off of Mela. Her primary defence should be evasion for one, and she seems like she might have a thing for ranged attacks and super high mobility.<br /> <br /> Her chosen also might offer some insight. They have Stealth, Lore, Occult, Thrown and Linguistics. That might help guide us towards how she acts socially and in combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T06:37:03-07:00","id":1344179,"title":"","content":"Idk.<br /> <br /> As the Children of Gaia, stating them is like trying to stat the Arrow Rain of Malfeas. 2E had the Dragons as a significant source of that element's Essence, and pegged them above the Greater Elemental Dragons (who were plot devices to be endured). <br /> <br /> I would certainly make Mela at 3CD level. At least 1/scene attack that does uncountable damage. <br /> <br /> The Elemental Dragons aren't potrayed as being socially adroit, but I certainly think a Defining Intimacy along the lines of &quot;I have earned this furlow&quot; is appropriate. I'd handle the social aspect as dice-light as possible. Just guide it based on stunts and Mela's Intimacies (and I like the idea of Righteous Lion Defence style protection of key Intimacies).<br /> <br /> For the sake of argument, I'd lean towards big dice pools over Charms, simply so I had less to keep track of. But I think fighting Mela is best done through negotiating environmental hazards -- like a Legendary Size Battle Group that spits out Bonfire Hazards instead of Withering attacks.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying &quot;don't do it&quot;, but I'm saying how do you stat the 23rd Crystal Orb that orbits SWLIHN, or the specific feeling of melancholy that strikes the citizens of Malfeas, or a being which is literally a constant rain of arrows from the sky, or the raging force of fire and destruction at the heart of the sun. Because these are the beings which are peers to Mela -- not second circle demons and lesser elemental dragons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T06:39:39-07:00","id":1344180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344168-help-me-stat-mela-the-elemental-dragon-of-air?p=1344171#post1344171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">#2 If she's initiating Fimbulwinter she\u2019ll probably be a significant cold based environmental hazard coupled with serious visibility penalties.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the sake of argument, I'd lean towards big dice pools over Charms, simply so I had less to keep track of. But I think fighting Mela is best done through negotiating environmental hazards</div> </div> </div> </div>Lots of environmental hazard stuff makes sense.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T07:37:00-07:00","id":1344188,"title":"","content":"A question I have is if they fight her or engage socially, are they just going to throw down, or do they have some kind of larger plan?<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve always felt that beings on the level of third circle demons or elemental dragons shouldn\u2019t be something that just gets fought straight up. More that you have to go on a journey to either dismantle some of their powers or collect specific knowledge and/or weapons that make it possible. For one there\u2019s a good chance Mela is going to have some serious backup in the forms of air based spirits, that\u2019s something your players may want to consider dealing with first.<br /> <br /> Looking through the Air aspected social charms, in social scenes Mela should be cold, calculating, but also idealistic. She is highly dedicated to principles over personal ties for her intimacies. She\u2019s also steeped in understanding, both able to make other understand with clarity and understand others herself.<br /> <br /> She should absolutely have legendary size, and I also agree with John that for the sake of running her she should probably have less charms which are more straightforward and powerful. Like she might have one that costs initiative and gives her an uncontested disengage. There\u2019s also just something about being a dragon that makes me want to give her some really good grapple abilities. <br /> <br /> Some of this also depends on how badass your players are. If you actually want them to be able to win reasonably or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T09:08:10-07:00","id":1344201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344168-help-me-stat-mela-the-elemental-dragon-of-air?p=1344188#post1344188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mela is going to have some serious backup in the forms of air based spirits, that\u2019s something your players may want to consider dealing with first.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, definitely. Thunderbirds, Huraka, Cloud People (though honestly they're not very powerful), Storm Serpents.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A question I have is if they fight her or engage socially, are they just going to throw down, or do they have some kind of larger plan? </div> </div> </div>Not currently. But then, they won't be fighting her next session; they've got to fly to her castle first, which means going through storms, past flying mountains, possibly being attacked by Fair Folk, not to mention there's some NPCs who are trying to get there as well for their own nefarious (or, possibly, heroic) ends.<br /> Then, when they get there, I hope they'll try and scope it out or something. But of course, if they go to talk to her first (which they generally do, and the Changing Moon has very good stats) they can't really make a surprise attack. Perhaps if negotiations fail they'll try something clever. But my guess is the Bull-Tiger will just punch her in the nose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T09:16:46-07:00","id":1344203,"title":"","content":"Stating the Elemental Dragons as Third Circle Demons would be the right thing to do as that is exactly what they are. Problem is that I dont thing 3e has any examples of Third Circle Demons to scale off of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T09:40:25-07:00","id":1344211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344168-help-me-stat-mela-the-elemental-dragon-of-air?p=1344201#post1344201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, definitely. Thunderbirds, Huraka, Cloud People (though honestly they're not very powerful), Storm Serpents.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I may offer more suggestions, spirit animals aren\u2019t out of the realm if possibility either. A spirit sparrow probably isn\u2019t worth worrying about, but I can definitely see a sky titan or something being involved.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344168-help-me-stat-mela-the-elemental-dragon-of-air?p=1344201#post1344201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not currently. But then, they won't be fighting her next session; they've got to fly to her castle first, which means going through storms, past flying mountains, possibly being attacked by Fair Folk, not to mention there's some NPCs who are trying to get there as well for their own nefarious (or, possibly, heroic) ends.<br /> Then, when they get there, I hope they'll try and scope it out or something. But of course, if they go to talk to her first (which they generally do, and the Changing Moon has very good stats) they can't really make a surprise attack. Perhaps if negotiations fail they'll try something clever. But my guess is the Bull-Tiger will just punch her in the nose.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s tough then...I want to suggest things that I would consider reasonable for an Essence 9 dragon god, but I don\u2019t want to suggest things that will just kill your players for engaging her either. <br /> <br /> Some other things I thought of are ranged attacks in the form of lightning strikes from her claws, and ways to vanish into the wind, reestablishing stealth in combat. <br /> <br /> Then again Mela doesn\u2019t necessarily need to kill her adversaries. If she has a good reason not to defeat doesn\u2019t necessarily mean death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T10:20:54-07:00","id":1344218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344168-help-me-stat-mela-the-elemental-dragon-of-air?p=1344203#post1344203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stating the Elemental Dragons as Third Circle Demons would be the right thing to do as that is exactly what they are. Problem is that I dont thing 3e has any examples of Third Circle Demons to scale off of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and part of the problem with that is the closest we have is probably Fakharu, and in my mind anyway the Elemental Dragons are solidly more badass than even directional censors, and also Fakarhu is really powerful, even alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T10:42:52-07:00","id":1344223,"title":"","content":"Have you done any fights with him? He seems weaker than Ahlat or Octavian, but I haven't actually seen him in action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T10:59:34-07:00","id":1344226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344168-help-me-stat-mela-the-elemental-dragon-of-air?p=1344223#post1344223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you done any fights with him? He seems weaker than Ahlat or Octavian, but I haven't actually seen him in action.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't, I might do one or two in the arena. To me with his stats he feels weaker than Octavian and Alhat, but he also fights differently, and a lot more cruelly. Basically, are you going to play him to win or not? Because if you are have him attack from the sky and breathe poison on everyone. Then swoop in and grab somebody, preferably the archer if there is one, and retreat back to the sky. Also if you can attack with a Might 2 battlegroup of spirits, and do it in a location that you can reflexively heal yourself in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T11:49:57-07:00","id":1344232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344168-help-me-stat-mela-the-elemental-dragon-of-air?p=1344203#post1344203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stating the Elemental Dragons as Third Circle Demons would be the right thing to do as that is exactly what they are. Problem is that I dont thing 3e has any examples of Third Circle Demons to scale off of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Third Circle Demons are the component souls of the Yozi.<br /> <br /> Gaia is not a Yozi and the Elemental Dragons are <i>explicitly</i> not her component souls (Third Circle Deva).<br /> <br /> The Five Elemental Dragons are Gaia's children. They're Primordial Behemoths like Kalmanka, Vitaris, Pellegrina, and Kamilla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T12:15:33-07:00","id":1344236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344168-help-me-stat-mela-the-elemental-dragon-of-air?p=1344232#post1344232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Five Elemental Dragons are Gaia's children. They're Primordial Behemoths like Kalmanka, Vitaris, Pellegrina, and Kamilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the latter has to be true for the former to be true.<br /> <br /> \u200b(I also don't think Adorjan's children are necessarily behemoths either.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T12:22:42-07:00","id":1344238,"title":"","content":"Do you guys think Raging Dragon Strike is compatible with Seven Venoms Exhalation? It IS an attack, and all RDS seems to require is that it be an attack to enhance it. That could make a huge difference","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T12:24:31-07:00","id":1344239,"title":"","content":"The elemental dragons are difficult to categorise entities somewhere between behemoths and gods, may have been Gaia's souls at some point in their existence, and may currently be the personifications of the elemental poles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T12:42:44-07:00","id":1344240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344168-help-me-stat-mela-the-elemental-dragon-of-air?p=1344232#post1344232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third Circle Demons are the component souls of the Yozi.<br /> <br /> Gaia is not a Yozi and the Elemental Dragons are <i>explicitly</i> not her component souls (Third Circle Deva).<br /> <br /> The Five Elemental Dragons are Gaia's children. They're Primordial Behemoths like Kalmanka, Vitaris, Pellegrina, and Kamilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>The distinction between Primordials and Yozi being purely political was always a good one. The distinction between demon and deva is the same, purely political. <br /> <br /> The Elemental Dragons changing to some form of Behemoth seems to me an entirely unnecessary and arbitrary change. Given I'm almost 100% certain that we will never see stats for one of the Elemental Dragons or any of Gaia's Third Circle Souls I'll go right ahead and ignore it.<br /> <br /> As for the question of how to stat an Elemental Dragon, you really need to determine what kind of story you're trying to tell. We dont really have any point of reference to work with, so needs of the story are what you have to use. Which happens to be the exact answer I give when asked &quot;how do you stat nukes?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T13:34:40-07:00","id":1344249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344168-help-me-stat-mela-the-elemental-dragon-of-air?p=1344240#post1344240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The distinction between Primordials and Yozi being purely political was always a good one. The distinction between demon and deva is the same, purely political.<br /> <br /> The Elemental Dragons changing to some form of Behemoth seems to me an entirely unnecessary and arbitrary change. Given I'm almost 100% certain that we will never see stats for one of the Elemental Dragons or any of Gaia's Third Circle Souls I'll go right ahead and ignore it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The arbitrary and unnecessary change was in making them beings comparable to third circle demons instead of the more nebulous title of &quot;Gaia's children&quot;, the latter being their description in the 1e core. I don't think anyone even considered that they were like Gaia's third circle souls until either Savant and Sorcerer or some highly optional adventures in Autochthonians entered print, the latter of which were full of highly questionable assumptions about the setting even without the above issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T14:17:52-07:00","id":1344254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">and the Elemental Dragons are <i>explicitly</i> not her component souls</div> </div> </div> </div>Where's that said? (Not saying you're wrong, I'm just wondering where it's explicitly stated they're not her component souls.)<br /> <br /> I honestly don't see why people find the idea that they're Gaia's third-circle Devas to be such an issue. No-one seems upset by Autocthon having 8 written-up Devas (who I think are pretty interesting and cool), so I don't see the issue with Gaia having five Devas reflecting the different elements that make up Creation.<br /> My impression is that people were just fed up with 2nd ed putting everything into boxes, rather than that it's a box they don't fit in.<br /> <br /> <br /> But it's also kind of irrelevant for my purposes; whether they are or not, they ought to be a fair bit more powerful than Ahlat, but not as much as a Primordial or the Unconquered Sun.<br /> Which probably ends up being about the same power you'd give to the third-circle devas of an extent Primordial anyway, regardless of whether they are or not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the question of how to stat an Elemental Dragon, you really need to determine what kind of story you're trying to tell. We dont really have any point of reference to work with, so needs of the story are what you have to use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heroes try to stop the apocalypse via talking down an angry dragon. And then if that doesn't work, have an epic fight to save the world against an immense millenia-old god-dragon, atop a floating ice palace beyond the edge of the world.<br /> (Or alternatively, if the No Moon's theory is correct, tricking the evil imposter into revealing where he's stashed the real Mela. I shouldn't really say whether that theory is wrong or not. No-one else seems convinced though.)<br /> <br /> I doubt they'll succeed at beating up an Elemental Dragon, but I feel that, for six Celestial Exalts, it shouldn't be utterly impossible. Just really hard (especially as she'll have a battle group of elementals plus a few elemental heroes, but maybe they can find a way past that). Very difficult (they're Essence 2 after all), but Mela's not as powerful as a Primordial, and the Celestial Exalted killed a whole bunch of them and hundreds of Third-Circle Devas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 10-28-2019, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T14:38:32-07:00","id":1344260,"title":"","content":"The Elemental Dragons created Exalted.<br /> <br /> They ought to be written up in a manner consistent with how one views beings of comparable power to the Celestial Incarnae, because that is the basic standard for being able to create Exalted.<br /> <br /> It really always had been, it just never needed to be stated before. Now we've got an Edition that has introduced more Exalted and has the premise of new kinds being made in the course of a story, so the standard needs to be more explicit.<br /> <br /> That also being a compelling argument for why they don't really function as Third Circle Demons (not powerful enough) or behemoths (not enough spiritual depth).<br /> <br /> So that's your starting point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T15:02:12-07:00","id":1344265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344168-help-me-stat-mela-the-elemental-dragon-of-air?p=1344254#post1344254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where's that said? (Not saying you're wrong, I'm just wondering where it's explicitly stated they're not her component souls.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Collected Word of God:<br /> To clarify, the Five Elemental Dragons are the Children of Gaia. They are not her souls. (John M\u00f8rke)<br /> Q: Huh. I'm cool with this.<br /> Does that make them little Primordials?<br /> Does that make them Elementals?<br /> Does that make them Gods?<br /> Does that make them Behemoths?<br /> Does that make them something else?<br /> Will we see Gaia's other Sub-souls detailed? (Daredevil)<br /> A: It makes them the Five Elemental Dragons. (Holden)<br /> <br /> Q: Pretty sure that given that, they fit best in the category of 'behemoths', but it's easy to posit them as sane Greater Elemental Dragons. (Requiem_Jeer)<br /> A: They are not behemoths. Behemoths are a particular thing, not a 'miscellaneous catch-all.' (Holden)<br /> <br /> Q: I'm getting a general feel of what Holden mentioned before about making Creation mysterious again. I see it in changes as the above mentioned status of elemental dragons in relation to Gaia, I believe this can be a way to diminish the &quot;category fever&quot; of 2e in which players discussed very specific aspects of the game at rediculous level.<br /> Am I getting this right? (Gonzo)<br /> A: Category fever suuuuuuuuuuuucks.<br /> What are the Five Elemental Dragons if they are not devas? They are the Five Elemental Dragons. (John M\u00f8rke)<br /> <br /> Vance: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/261914-the-lie-of-the-immaculate-dragons?p=263253#post263253\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...253#post263253</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T15:08:40-07:00","id":1344268,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry but Behemoth is very much a miscellaneous catch-all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T15:24:40-07:00","id":1344270,"title":"","content":"Thanks John. I think Morke went a bit far there as a reaction to the previous edition, but then... it just doesn't matter all that much.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm sorry but Behemoth is very much a miscellaneous catch-all.</div> </div> </div> </div> <br /> Eh, you wouldn't use it for all the various wacky monsters in Hundred Devils. Only the giant, powerful stuff.<br /> <br /> I'd say it's fairly miscellaneous, but not actually catch-<i>all</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T15:29:28-07:00","id":1344271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344168-help-me-stat-mela-the-elemental-dragon-of-air?p=1344268#post1344268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry but Behemoth is very much a miscellaneous catch-all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually the 1E Corebook is surprisingly specific:<br /> <br /> &quot;Great beasts containing fragments of raw Wyld Essence&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344168-help-me-stat-mela-the-elemental-dragon-of-air?p=1344270#post1344270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks John. I think Morke went a bit far there as a reaction to the previous edition, but then... it just doesn't matter all that much.</div> </div> </div> </div>John said it, and Holden said it, and Vance said it.<br /> <br /> At this point, unless Eric or Grabowski want to weigh in, it's a settled matter.<br /> <br /> The first time the Five Elemental Dragons are mentioned in Exalted, it's as the progenitors of the Dragon-Blooded. The second time (a few pages later) it's as the children of Gaia. The third time, it's their enemies (specifically the Elemental Dragons' enemies, not &quot;the gods' enemies&quot;) who levied the Great Curse (at this point the Yozi have already been introduced by name).<br /> <br /> Grabowski lays out a clear vision of the Dragons as Gaia's children. That's not the same as explicitly denying they're also her souls (and as you say, it really makes very little difference -- both to the game and to this scenario), but this certainly isn't a &quot;new thing&quot; or an ex-dev going on his own bizarre tangent.<br /> <br /> In canon the Five Elemental Dragons are Gaia's children. Then again, literally Exalted's first rule was &quot;if you don't like it, change it&quot;, so &quot;canon&quot; is of dubious value here.<br /> <br /> (I feel bad for quoting Wizard then making a post which was only tangentially related to what I was quoting. So apologies for that segway.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 10-28-2019, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T15:52:56-07:00","id":1344283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344168-help-me-stat-mela-the-elemental-dragon-of-air?p=1344260#post1344260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Elemental Dragons created Exalted.<br /> <br /> They ought to be written up in a manner consistent with how one views beings of comparable power to the Celestial Incarnae, because that is the basic standard for being able to create Exalted.<br /> <br /> It really always had been, it just never needed to be stated before. Now we've got an Edition that has introduced more Exalted and has the premise of new kinds being made in the course of a story, so the standard needs to be more explicit.<br /> <br /> That also being a compelling argument for why they don't really function as Third Circle Demons (not powerful enough) or behemoths (not enough spiritual depth).</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking about saying something very similar to this. The Five Elemental Dragons empowered the Dragonblooded Exalted in much the same way as The Five Maidens empowered the Sidereal Exalted. Treat Mela and any interactions/conflicts with her the same way you would with Mars or Venus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T16:07:54-07:00","id":1344291,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's the bottom line really. Whatever they are, they are beings on-par with the less powerful of the incarnae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T16:12:22-07:00","id":1344293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344168-help-me-stat-mela-the-elemental-dragon-of-air?p=1344254#post1344254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">whether they are or not, they ought to be a fair bit more powerful than Ahlat, but not as much as a Primordial or the Unconquered Sun.<br /> Which probably ends up being about the same power you'd give to the third-circle devas of an extent Primordial anyway, regardless of whether they are or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Unconquered Sun is still modelled as being kind of invincible, then sure.<br /> <br /> There are issues with the write-up in Glories in its own right and transplanting to Third Edition, but using it as a reference point I feel as though there's something to starting with the Sun's mass destruction effects.<br /> <br /> Maybe a number of powers based around the image of a being that summons hurricanes to deal with problems. The picture in my head is that if you approach the Elemental Dragon of Air* and they find you bothersome, one of their powers will be becoming surrounded by a cyclone to fling you away like an insect. A bit like one of the powers of that five-dot armour, but stronger and of a larger scope. That particular one also following the image of the intellectual side of Air; the Dragon does not want to be bothered by distractions.<br /> <br /> I'm also thinking something resembling the power of Stormcaller for offence, but detached from the need to be good with a daiklave and not so much with the options for concentrating the power against a single opponent. The Dragon is not incapable of fighting one on one, but much of their power is not following that image and persona.<br /> <br /> Still, they are dragons, and there is that work named for them... I'm also suddenly thinking about those really cool dragons in Breath of the Wild... I propose that in addition to large elemental and spiritual manifestations, each Dragon has a Claw, Horn, Fang and Scale to convey that they're not just transcend numinous beings, but capital-d dragons; fierce and bestial, carnivores of the world before world. Two or three powers to represent terrible crushing, rending powers that their appendages might bring down upon real annoyances or prey, one or two special defensive or durability options.<br /> <br /> * At some point I found myself kind of &quot;eh&quot; about giving the actual Elemental Dragons the exact names of the mythical Immaculate Dragons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T16:42:50-07:00","id":1344299,"title":"","content":"I think officially they aren't actually called the same as the immaculate dragons.<br /> <br /> In practice it's probably more &quot;I guess these are their names now&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T03:15:16-07:00","id":1344367,"title":"","content":"It could make sense for them to have the same names; the original preachers/compilers/constructors of the Immaculate religion naming their (constructed) messiahs after the Elemental Dragons, as part of an attempt at legitimacy. Most new monotheistic religions still call their supreme deity &quot;God&quot;, because it makes them look more mainstream.<br /> <br /> If they're not, then that would presumably either be because a)Dragonblood scholars didn't know the names of the Elemental Dragons (possible but unlikely), b)the Elemental Dragons don't actually have names, c)the Sidereals thought it would irritate the real Elemental Dragons to use their names, so made up names for the Immaculate Dragons, d)their true names are considered too holy to be known by mortals or the unitiated, and only the Mouth of Peace and top Immaculates actually know their real names.<br /> <br /> It could also be that it's just different languages. I say God, my Chinese friends say Shengdi, Syrian Christians say Maryah Alaha, in Hebrew it's YHWH, etc. Adonia, El, El Shadai, Jehovah, Allah. Which one is &quot;right&quot;? I don't think there really is a single &quot;correct&quot; one.<br /> <br /> Maybe Hesiesh, Sextis Jylis, Mela, Daana'd and Pasiap are the old Earthtongue forms of the Dragons' names, and their real names (in Old Realm, I guess) are different.<br /> <br /> In the game I run, where no PC has Occult or Lore 5 or a background at a famous university or something (the one mental character is a swamp shaman), and they mostly just speak Skytongue (the shaman also speaks Old Realm, the merchant also speaks Riverspeak and Guild Cant), the names of the Dragons are mostly confused and mixed. They've heard talk about Sutr, ruler of Muspelheim; is that Hesiesh? Is it not? They've heard that Jormungundr, the World Serpent, is causing earthquakes. Is that Pasiap? Gaia? Different gods, elementals, Raksha, locals, Dragonblood who may be Dynasts or from the Shogunate, etc, all use different and confusing terms. I only stuck with Mela for the Air Dragon, because I felt that being the Air Dragon, people in the North-North-East would have a more consistent way to talk about her than they would the Fire Dragon or Water Dragon.<br /> Not, of course, that cultures present her consistently. The Raksha described her as the Dragon Queen of Wind and Frost, daughter of Jormungundr and Granddaughter of the giant Ymir, whose bones and blood make the earth. The Dragonblood who were the main antagonists for the first story arc talked about her as a (human-shaped) warrior-scholar. The peasantry consider her the Queen of the court of Winter Gods.<br /> But they all called her Mela whether in Skytongue or Old Realm (partly so the PCs don't get confused; I want them to be a bit confused, but not too much!).<br /> <br /> Now whether she calls herself Mela when the PCs meet her... I think even if she doesn't consider that her name (I imagine her actually using some extremely conceptual thing for her name, like a particular roar of Air, or maybe a string of complex syllables with deep meaning in Old Realm), if she's speaking (or roaring wind?) in Skytongue, she may answer to Mela because, well, that's what mortals call her. Maybe depends how irritatable and arrogant she's feeling.<br /> <br /> Like, when I lived in China the second time, my teacher called me \u6b27\u5b50, and that's fine. My friend Liu has 3 names; his Mandarin name (Liu), his Manchurian name (Aisin Giorio), and his English name (Sherlock). No problem, no insult.<br /> But then, we're not Dragons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 10-29-2019, 06:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T03:43:23-07:00","id":1344376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344168-help-me-stat-mela-the-elemental-dragon-of-air?p=1344293#post1344293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the Unconquered Sun is still modelled as being kind of invincible, then sure.<br /> <br /> There are issues with the write-up in Glories in its own right and transplanting to Third Edition, but using it as a reference point I feel as though there's something to starting with the Sun's mass destruction effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine he'd be written differently and... sort of less powerful (I know some people who played very high-level optimised paranoia-combat-orientated characters found him rather weak). But I don't really have any 3rd edition upper bound for Exalted power.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I think mass-destruction effects seem appropriate for Elemental Dragons. I can well imagine that, say, the Elemental Dragon of Air can initiate Fimbulwinter, summon lightning storms, blow an entire army far away, etc... but this doesn't necessarily mean she has a Perfect Dodge or Overwhelming negator.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The picture in my head is that if you approach the Elemental Dragon of Air* and they find you bothersome, one of their powers will be becoming surrounded by a cyclone to fling you away like an insect. A bit like one of the powers of that five-dot armour, but stronger and of a larger scope. That particular one also following the image of the intellectual side of Air; the Dragon does not want to be bothered by distractions. </div> </div> </div>I like that. Which armour do you mean?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm also thinking something resembling the power of Stormcaller for offence, but detached from the need to be good with a daiklave and not so much with the options for concentrating the power against a single opponent. </div> </div> </div>The lightning storm-type stuff? Yeah, that works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Dragon is not incapable of fighting one on one, but much of their power is not following that image and persona. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think that's both fitting and the most practical way for me to run the fight. It's also the most dramatic and exciting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Two or three powers to represent terrible crushing, rending powers that their appendages might bring down upon real annoyances or prey, one or two special defensive or durability options. </div> </div> </div>I think these are probably the ones I can easily build from Fakharu and the Storm Serpent. Maybe just buff up them a bit, or keep the charm the same (the Storm Serpent's defensive charm gives +2 Evasion and halves Withering Damage, that's pretty good) but with better base stats (attack pools, soak, etc).<br /> <br /> I would like to follow John's earlier advice, of having a few really powerful charms rather than lots of small ones, just for ease. Like the way Ahlat/Octavian/Fakharu/the Nemissary/the volcano behemoth are built.<br /> <br /> (Not that these necessarily reflect the breadth of her powers, but rather the breadth of powers likely to come up in the game. Her ability to understand where winds are across Creation, and what's affecting the winds, probably doesn't need to be written up.)<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T03:44:32-07:00","id":1344377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344168-help-me-stat-mela-the-elemental-dragon-of-air?p=1344283#post1344283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was thinking about saying something very similar to this. The Five Elemental Dragons empowered the Dragonblooded Exalted in much the same way as The Five Maidens empowered the Sidereal Exalted. Treat Mela and any interactions/conflicts with her the same way you would with Mars or Venus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I was thinking of that earlier, it seems about right. I mean, not that they are similar; Venus's powers, personality, and form, and conceptually extremely different from an Elemental Dragon.<br /> <br /> But more than Ahlat, less than the Unconquered Sun or a Primordial, still seems right. My point about Third-Circle Demons... probably is irrelevant, as we've got no examples of a 3rd circle Demon for 3rd edition anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T03:47:02-07:00","id":1344378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Actually the 1E Corebook is surprisingly specific:<br /> <br /> &quot;Great beasts containing fragments of raw Wyld Essence&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>What about the behemoths made by Primordials though? I'm not sure they necessarily contain fragments of raw Wyld Essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T05:24:08-07:00","id":1344389,"title":"","content":"I don't think that saying the incarnae, elemental dragons and third circle demons are all <i>roughly </i>in the same ballpark of power is inaccurate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T05:31:08-07:00","id":1344392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344168-help-me-stat-mela-the-elemental-dragon-of-air?p=1344367#post1344367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most new monotheistic religions still call their supreme deity &amp;quot;God&amp;quot;, because it makes them look more mainstream.</div> </div> </div> </div>God is just a word; do they make their object of worship the Tetragrammaton? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344168-help-me-stat-mela-the-elemental-dragon-of-air?p=1344367#post1344367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could also be that it's just different languages. I say God, my Chinese friends say Shengdi, Syrian Christians say Maryah Alaha, in Hebrew it's YHWH, etc. Adonia, El, El Shadai, Jehovah, Allah. Which one is &amp;quot;right&amp;quot;? I don't think there really is a single &amp;quot;correct&amp;quot; one.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, God is not the name of the focus of those religions in English, it's just a noun. Nor is it Allah in Islam, that's just the noun in Arabic; Arab Christians also use the term. Christianity and Islam both hold that the Tetragrammaton (read as Yahweh in English and Jehovah in Latin) is God's name, while Hebrew speakers won't actually address their God as that; they use terms such as Elohim (which is the generic Hebrew term for deities) or HaShem (which just means &quot;the Name&quot;).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dragonblood who were the main antagonists for the first story arc talked about her as a (human-shaped) warrior-scholar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon Blooded from the Realm? How have they grown up and gotten away with such heresy?<br /> <br /> I'm all for the principle you're bringing with variety and ambiguity in names (and not just for divinities; of Dynasts are well traveled and often far from home, I think it's worth having them mediate scenarios of dealing with people that find their names difficult to pronounce, and accepting local substitutes).<br /> <br /> My issue with a point having been reached at which the fanbase and writing (although I'm not sure which came first, or if the latter ever showed up in a book rather than an Ink Monkeys article) conflated the original Immaculate Dragon names with the Elemental Dragons is that I find it reductive, lazy and ambiguous in the not good way. I think it weakens the mythology of the Immaculate Dragons, the characteristics ascribed to them, when it carries the implication of them being stand ins for the actually existing beings in a way that makes people approach them as though they have those traits, or the traits become kind of overshadowed or forgotten in comparison to the true Dragons.<br /> <br /> I think it hurts the presentation of the Immaculate religion to give too much reality to its mythic hero figures, because I think it shifts focus away on their significance as idealised figures of emulation and inspiration. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344168-help-me-stat-mela-the-elemental-dragon-of-air?p=1344376#post1344376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">this doesn't necessarily mean she has a Perfect Dodge</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, neither do Solars really, not in the manner of the old standards and terminology. Sure they've got a Dodge Charm that is now their one and only way of totally and effortlessly negating any incoming attack, but it can only be used once in a scene being fulfilling the fighty conditions of resetting it.<br /> <br /> So a being that isn't really being modelled as a Kung Fu fighter could still be granted a power to negate enemy attacks which resolves in a mechanically identical way, but has different costs and reset conditions and it comes across as something deriving from the grandeur and energy of one of the highest divinities, rather than dodging well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like that. Which armour do you mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>The one in Arms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I think that's both fitting and the most practical way for me to run the fight. It's also the most dramatic and exciting.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think these are probably the ones I can easily build from Fakharu and the Storm Serpent. Maybe just buff up them a bit, or keep the charm the same (the Storm Serpent's defensive charm gives +2 Evasion and halves Withering Damage, that's pretty good) but with better base stats (attack pools, soak, etc).<br /> <br /> I would like to follow John's earlier advice, of having a few really powerful charms rather than lots of small ones, just for ease. Like the way Ahlat/Octavian/Fakharu/the Nemissary/the volcano behemoth are built.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing I recall in descriptions of Ahlat and Octavian is that they're built with fighting styles that are very narrow, but strong; I recall the description being that the former is built to deliver legal alpha strikes (with a potential to essentially get another alpha strike in of he can keep going long enough after the real one failed), and the latter for absorbing lots of punishment and turning it back on his attacker. Lack of other Charms means they don't have anything outside that range, bit what they get gives it some intricacy and sophistication.<br /> <br /> The volcanic behemoth gets Merits and powers that give fighting it particular characteristics; it's built to be something that has to be broken down gradually with a capacity to rebuild itself and where inflicting that damage results in it spewing lava all over.<br /> <br /> So if being approached in a combative manner, for a being of that significance I think it's worth having an encounter that is especially fraught even if not like fighting something humanoid. I don't think that requires a lot of Charms, just a core idea of what the shape of the battle and the conditions for winning or losing are.<br /> <br /> I'm suddenly thinking of something like what powerful Artifacts get, a distinct mechanic that builds up as smaller achievements are made, and can be used to power a kind of finisher. Now it's crossing over with the image of Elemental Aura being part of an inheritance from the Dragons, although altered to fit the mixture of five and human activities; in the individual Dragons, more like something with stages, with something that can end the fight requiring the top stage. I wonder what would serve as a suitably air-themed process for that to build up.<br /> <br /> I think that encountering such a being even socially should have its challenges and perils thought out for players who would take that route. I'm thinking the form of the engagement would be something like the challenge of figuring out what could be the Intimacies of such an entity, with some Charms to both model the difficulty of reading something so divine and alien and maybe something that can kind of emotionally and psychically overwhelm the person who tries (and tries to leverage what they find).<br /> <br /> Mind, I'm also thinking that a challenge in either approach could be preventing the Dragon from getting bored or annoyed and simply leaving. If one is going for simplicity then it's fine to ascribe an ego that would stick around for pride or offence, but I think it could be fun to give the approach some preamble in the form of players needing to come up with something that invests the Dragon in sticking around to do anything with you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Not that these necessarily reflect the breadth of her powers, but rather the breadth of powers likely to come up in the game. Her ability to understand where winds are across Creation, and what's affecting the winds, probably doesn't need to be written up.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Your Fimbulwinter sounds in that boat, really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T05:41:38-07:00","id":1344393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344168-help-me-stat-mela-the-elemental-dragon-of-air?p=1344378#post1344378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the behemoths made by Primordials though? I'm not sure they necessarily contain fragments of raw Wyld Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>3E redefines Behemoths on page 117:<br /> <br /> &quot;These are behemoths, discarded by the ancient world-makers who created them, immortal half-formed prototypes of the later life that would walk the face of Creation [...] Properly, behemoths are the byblows of a Creation that never happened [...] As it is difficult for the average person to inquire into the origins of the walking nightmare devouring their family or destroying their city, the word \u201cbehemoth\u201d is often also misapplied&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 10-29-2019, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T07:12:28-07:00","id":1344408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344168-help-me-stat-mela-the-elemental-dragon-of-air?p=1344389#post1344389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that saying the incarnae, elemental dragons and third circle demons are all <i>roughly </i>in the same ballpark of power is inaccurate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do. Third Circle Demons are powerful, but they tend to be focused on a very specific and narrow form of power, even up to the level of described fetich souls. <br /> <br /> The Incarnae have a higher standing in mythology, they intersect with some early developer statements about only a select few gods being numinous and transcendent, and then we got a more firm picture of the Maidens of Destiny exercising power integral to the functioning of the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T21:03:47-07:00","id":1344572,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I would start with a cool idea for the encounter you have and work backward. This is a being somewhere between a 3CD and an Incarna, primary influence on Creation's Essence, and on top of that you've already established that some weird shit is going down.<br /> <br /> If it were me, I'd probably say something about most of Mela's power going into creating/maintaining/being the apocalyptic winter currently ravaging Creation, such that the incarnation they actually interact with is more... relatable. Maybe something on the order of a super-powerful Dragonblooded (Mela's Immaculate self) at the heart of a raging storm and commanding a battlegroup of Storm Serpents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T01:05:00-07:00","id":1344600,"title":"","content":"I don't think I would make her a Dragonblood (the Immaculate Philosophy isn't true; she has no Immaculate form), but thinking about the encounter first is probably a good way to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T01:25:28-07:00","id":1344606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344168-help-me-stat-mela-the-elemental-dragon-of-air?p=1344600#post1344600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think I would make her a Dragonblood (the Immaculate Philosophy isn't true; she has no Immaculate form), but thinking about the encounter first is probably a good way to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be clear:<br /> <br /> The Unconquered Sun's form was a Dragon King with infinite arms, until the Exalted won the Primordial War then he looked like a four-armed man. Lesser Elemental Dragons can take human form. The Primordials have jouten forms like the Brass Dancer.<br /> <br /> The Immaculate Philosophy doesn't have to be true for Mela to have a humanoid form. Nor is Mela's power infinite, even with a dead sibling the other Dragon's Essence should be opposing an eternal winter. And a humanoid is probably easier to impersonate than a dragon.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying you have to use this idea (think of the first encounter and do what you think tells a good story). Just saying the Immaculate Philosophy doesn't have to be true to use this idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T05:50:40-07:00","id":1344640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344168-help-me-stat-mela-the-elemental-dragon-of-air?p=1344600#post1344600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think I would make her a Dragonblood (the Immaculate Philosophy isn't true; she has no Immaculate form), but thinking about the encounter first is probably a good way to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't making a theological statement, I was coming from a place of &quot;if you want stats for a fightable humanoid form of an elemental dragon, well, there's this entire book right over there full of combat charms, some of which are <i>named after her</i>, belonging to elemental-themed Exalted who claim descent from her... maybe start there for mechanics?&quot;<br /> <br /> And it just so happens that <s>a no good lying sidereal</s> some theologians say that such a thing, a fightable humanoid incarnation of Mela The Elemental Dragon of Air who used Dragonblooded powers, existed before, and called her &quot;Mela The Immaculate Dragon of Air&quot;. So I was using that as a shorthand to convey my meaning.<br /> <br /> I also think it's more interesting if the Philosophy has some connection to reality, however tenuous. And maybe if you actually get to meet @TheRealMela, that's a good time to learn what it was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 10-30-2019, 08:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T07:36:15-07:00","id":1344655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Immaculate Philosophy doesn't have to be true for Mela to have a humanoid form.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true. Most Elemental Dragons can take a humanoid form.<br /> And Blackwell does make a good (and very tempting) point about already-written mechanics. (Though one could argue they're a bit weak; even an essence 5 Dragonblood is probably going to lose hard to six essence 2 Lunars. Though maybe not when backed up by a battle group of elementals).<br /> <br /> But a giant Dragon is a more dramatic and epic fight. I think adapting some Dragonblood charms to stick on to the Dragon is a good idea though (maybe say she's perpetually in Air Aura to boost them a bit), just for ease of use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T07:57:16-07:00","id":1344663,"title":"","content":"I don't think Terrestrial Exalted Charms are nearly powerful enough for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T08:21:04-07:00","id":1344947,"title":"","content":"I think the Giant Dragon Fight is a perfectly good option as well. If it's really a dramatic setpiece and not just a tough encouter, I think you're looking at something more like a Juggernaught battle, though. Different zones, special multi-stage gambits, environmental hazards, human-scale supporting cast to do 'traditional' combat with as everything else is going on...<br /> <br /> I figure if you *really* want to commit to the bit, Mela the Elemental Dragon of Air is going to be miles long and that makes her as much the location as the opponent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 10-31-2019, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T08:57:12-07:00","id":1344954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344168-help-me-stat-mela-the-elemental-dragon-of-air?p=1344947#post1344947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Giant Dragon Fight is a perfectly good option as well. If it's really a dramatic setpiece and not just a tough encouter, I think you're looking at something more like a Juggernaught battle, though. Different zones, special multi-stage gambits, environmental hazards, human-scale supporting cast to do 'traditional' combat with as everything else is going on...<br /> <br /> I figure if you *really* want to commit to the bit, Mela the Elemental Dragon of Air is going to be miles long and that makes her as much the location as the opponent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that'd probably make it feel more epic. And it'd give people a chance to use stuff like different excellencies, survival charms, that kind of thing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T11:14:24-07:00","id":1344993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344168-help-me-stat-mela-the-elemental-dragon-of-air?p=1344947#post1344947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figure if you *really* want to commit to the bit, Mela the Elemental Dragon of Air is going to be miles long and that makes her as much the location as the opponent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. I'd feel robbed if fighting the friggin Elemental Dragon of Air was just another swordfight with a humanoid manifestation. Even in a game like Exalted, how often do you get to bring in an encounter with a miles-long dragon? <br /> <br /> (I ran an encounter like that in a Mutants and Masterminds fantasy game. The party had to spend the first ten rounds using the space-mage's portals to leapfrog their way along her body while she tried to shake them off, rained thunderstorms on them, dove into the ocean, etc.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T11:26:04-07:00","id":1344999,"title":"","content":"Ooh, I like that. Try and run along to the head maybe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T12:54:15-07:00","id":1345030,"title":"","content":"Personally, for an encounter this significant, I'd recommend taking some cues from video games - when they want to make a boss fight really epic, multiple stages with different gameplay styles are the thing. So you could have the first &quot;phase&quot; be meeting the apparently-humanoid Mela, surrounded by her court of elementals and weather gods and such. If the players fight her in this version, running her as an Essence 5 DB sounds like a good approach. Once the players have knocked down her HLs a bit (down to, say, the back half of her -2s), she transforms into an elemental dragon (I'd use Fakharu's corebook stats, but with more air-related powers, and just generally upgraded stats). Then, if they manage to actually take <i>that</i> down, the body dissolves... only to reveal that its tail was always sort of connected to the vast river of clouds that the whole thing was set on, which has now begun to <i>move</i>. The &quot;body&quot; the PCs defeated was just a fragment of Mela's power and form, and now they've got the attention of the whole thing. Now, it's a running battle along Mela's miles-long actual body, being attacked by more members of her court, and Mela's own appendages, each of which is a legendary-sized thing in itself. <i>Finally</i>, when they've defeated enough of those, they reach the head, which is its own legendary-sized fight, plus minions, <i>plus</i> assorted environmental hazards doing uncountable damage. <br /> <br /> If you run it like that, and you <i>don't</i> want either Mela or the PCs dead, I would definitely advise giving them <i>lots</i> of opportunities to end the fight early and descalate things. Fortunately, if you run Mela as the archtypical Air-Aspected DB, that's pretty plausible. If she's super-calculating and subtle, she could quite plausibly be repeatedly be saying things like &quot;good, you've proved your worth. Now, cease this pointless fighting, and I will aid you in your <i>true</i> quest...&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T13:25:03-07:00","id":1345040,"title":"","content":"I do love ultimate forms...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T13:42:15-07:00","id":1345044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344168-help-me-stat-mela-the-elemental-dragon-of-air?p=1344999#post1344999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooh, I like that. Try and run along to the head maybe.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want I can try to dig up my notes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}